rom `@cyntler/react-doc-viewer` (line 310) — this handles **image + PDF** rendering. No `<audio>` player exists anywhere in the app; audio falls through to DocViewer or is unavailable. No dedicated image component in this flow.\n- Helpers: `isPrivateUrl` (line 131), `MIME_TYPE_MAPPING`.\n\n### `VideoPreview`\n`modules/activities/files/components/VideoPreview.tsx:17`\n```ts\ntype VideoPreviewProps = { videoName: string; videoUrl: string };\nexport const VideoPreview\n```\nNative `<video controls>`; on error shows `UnavailableFilePreview`.\n\n### `UnavailableFilePreview` — fallback card with download\n`modules/activities/files/components/UnavailableFilePreview.tsx:38`\n```ts\ntype UnavailableFilePreviewProps = { fileName: string; fileUrl: string; message: ReactNode };\n```\n\n### `CallRecordingVideoPlayer` (separate, richer video player)\n`modules/page-layout/widgets/call-recording-transcript/components/CallRecordingVideoPlayer.tsx:88`\n```ts\ntype CallRecordingVideoPlayerProps = { ref?: Ref<HTMLVideoElement>; src: string; onRetry: () => Promise<unknown> };\n```\nFirst-frame buffering overlay, playback-error + retry. URL helper: `call-recording/utils/getCallRecordingVideoFileUrl.ts:4` — `getCallRecordingVideoFileUrl(callRecording): string | undefined`. Used by `CallRecordingTranscriptBody.tsx:101`.\n\n### `fetchCsvPreview` (CSV parser)\n`modules/activities/files/utils/fetchCsvPreview.ts:10` — `fetchCsvPreview(url): Promise<{ headers: string[]; rows: string[][] }>` (papaparse, 50 rows).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Preview modal / card components\n\n### `GlobalFilePreviewModal` — global modal, driven by Jotai atom\n`modules/ui/field/display/components/GlobalFilePreviewModal.tsx:75` — mounted app-wide at `modules/app/components/WorkspaceAppProviders.tsx:79`.\n- Reads/writes `filePreviewState` (`modules/ui/field/display/states/filePreviewState.ts:4`): `createAtomState<FieldFilesValue | null>({ key: 'filePreviewState', defaultValue: null })`.\n- Opens on `filePreview` set, header title/download (`downloadFile`), lazy `DocumentViewer`, passes `documentName/documentUrl/documentExtension`. This is the \"attachment preview modal\" primitive reused by field displays.\n\n### `AttachmentList` — local preview modal (records page)\n`modules/activities/files/components/AttachmentList.tsx:96`\n```ts\ntype AttachmentListProps = { targetableObject: ActivityTargetableObject; attachments: Attachment[] };\nexport const AttachmentList\nexport const PREVIEW_MODAL_ID = 'preview-modal'; // line 94\n```\nOwns its own `ModalStatefulWrapper` (`:179`), downloads via `getAttachmentUrl`, renders `DocumentViewer`. Also handles drag-drop upload (see §5).\n\n### Chip / card triggers\n- `modules/ui/field/display/components/FilesDisplay.tsx:19` — `FilesDisplay({ value?: FieldFilesValue[], forceDisableClick?, isUploadWindowOpen?, isFileUploading? })`. On click either downloads (if preview disabled) or sets `filePreviewState`. Renders `UploadFileChip` while uploading/empty.\n- `modules/ui/field/display/components/FileChip.tsx:24` — `FileChip({ file: FieldFilesValue, onClick, forceDisableClick? })`, uses `FileIcon`, handles `isDeleted`.\n- `modules/ui/field/display/components/UploadFileChip.tsx:47` — `UploadFileChip({ isLoading = true })`, spinner/arrow placeholder chip.\n- `modules/ai/components/internal/AgentChatFilePreview.tsx:25` — `AgentChatFilePreview({ file: ExtendedFileUIPart | File, onRemove?, isUploading? })`, pushes into `filePreviewState`.\n- `modules/file/components/AttachmentChip.tsx:64` — `AttachmentChip({ file: {id,name}, onRemove, readonly? })` (email attachments).\n- `modules/settings/legal/components/DpaDocumentPreview.tsx` (DPA-specific, not generic).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Fallback file icon by mime/extension\n\n### `FileIcon` — main icon component\n`modules/file/components/FileIcon.tsx:46`\n```ts\ntype FileIconProps = { fileCategory: AttachmentFileCategory | FileCategory; size?: 'small'|'medium'; thumbnailUrl?: string };\nexport const FileIcon\n```\n- Renders `<img>` thumbnail for `IMAGE` category when `thumbnailUrl` present (falls back to icon on error), else `AvatarOrIcon`/styled icon.\n- Icon map `modules/file/utils/fileIconMappings.ts:14` — `IconMapping: Record<AttachmentFileCategory, IconComponent>` (ARCHIVE→IconFileZip, AUDIO→IconHeadphones, IMAGE→IconPhoto, PRESENTATION→IconPresentation, SPREADSHEET→IconTable, TEXT_DOCUMENT→IconFileText, VIDEO→IconVideo, OTHER→IconFile).\n- Colors `modules/file/hooks/useFileCategoryColors.ts:8` — `useFileCategoryColors(): Record<AttachmentFileCategory, string>` (also overrides from metadata `fileCategory` options). Sibling `useFileIconColors` in `modules/file/hooks/`.\n\n### Extension → category maps (two exist)\n- `modules/activities/files/utils/getFileType.ts:63` — `getFileType(fileName): AttachmentFileCategory` (large extension→category map, line 3).\n- `modules/object-record/record-field/ui/utils/getFileCategoryFromExtension.ts:3` — `getFileCategoryFromExtension(extension?): FileCategory` (subset, used by `FileChip`/`AgentChatFilePreview`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Upload flows (hooks, signatures, drag-drop, file picker)\n\n### Core low-level upload (pre-signed URL, 3-step)\n`modules/file/hooks/useDirectFileUpload.ts:16`\n```ts\ntype DirectFileUploadOptions = { fileFolder: FileFolder; fieldMetadataId?: string; signal?: AbortSignal };\nexport const useDirectFileUpload = () => ({ uploadFile: (file: File, opts) => Promise<FileWithSignedUrl> });\n```\nCalls `createFileUpload` → HTTP PUT to `uploadTarget.uploadUrl` → `completeFileUpload`. `signal` supports abort (none of the callers below pass one → no cancel UI). Mutations: `modules/file/graphql/mutations/createFileUpload.ts`, `completeFileUpload.ts`. Snackbars on success/failure only, no progress or retry.\n\n### Attachment flows\n- `modules/activities/files/hooks/useUploadAttachmentFile.tsx:12` — `{ uploadAttachmentFile: (file: File, targetableObject: ActivityTargetableObject) => Promise<{ attachmentAbsoluteURL: string; attachmentFileId: string }> }` (uploads to `FileFolder.FilesField` then `createOneRecord` Attachment).\n- `modules/activities/files/hooks/useUploadAttachmentFiles.ts:4` — `{ uploadAttachmentFiles: ({ files: File[]; targetableObject }) => Promise<void> }` (sequential loop).\n- `modules/activities/files/hooks/useCanUploadAttachmentFiles.ts:6` — `useCanUploadAttachmentFiles(targetableObject) => { canUploadFiles: boolean }` (permission `UPLOAD_FILE` + record update).\n- `modules/activities/files/hooks/useAttachments.tsx:6` — `useAttachments(targetableObject) => { attachments, loading, totalCountAttachments }`.\n- `modules/activities/files/hooks/useAttachFileRelatedRecordAction.tsx:14` — `useAttachFileRelatedRecordAction({ targetRecord, onUploadComplete? }): RelatedRecordActionBinding` (hidden input trigger).\n- `modules/object-record/record-field/ui/meta-types/hooks/useUploadFilesFieldFile.ts:9` — `{ uploadFile: (file: File, fieldMetadataId: string) => Promise<FieldFilesValue> }` (for FILES field, `FileFolder.FilesField`; success/error snackbars).\n- `modules/object-record/record-field/ui/meta-types/utils/uploadMultipleFiles.ts:4` — `uploadMultipleFiles(files, fieldMetadataId, uploadFile): Promise<FieldFilesValue[]>` (sequential).\n- `modules/object-record/record-field/ui/meta-types/input/components/FilesFieldInput.tsx:24` — the FILES field input; calls `useFileUpload().openFileUpload`, enforces `maxNumberOfValues` with an error snackbar (`:88`), previews via `filePreviewState` (`:160`).\n\n### Drag-drop components\n- `modules/activities/files/components/DropZone.tsx:48` — `DropZone({ setIsDraggingFile, onUploadFiles: (files: File[]) => void })`. Uses `react-dropzone`; `maxSize: maxFileSize` from `useSpreadsheetImportInternal()` (shared spreadsheet config, **not** the attachment/email limit); no `onDropRejected` handler → oversized drops are silently ignored here.\n- `modules/spreadsheet-import/steps/components/UploadStep/components/DropZone.tsx:114` — `DropZone({ onContinue, isLoading })`; `maxSize: maxFileSize`, `onDropRejected` shows a detailed snackbar (`:136-147`), `accept` xls/xlsx/csv.\n- `modules/activities/files/components/FilesCardContent.tsx:40` — drag-enter guard + `DropZone`; empty state `AnimatedPlaceholder type=\"noFile\"` + `AttachmentUploadTrigger`.\n- `modules/activities/files/components/FilesCard.tsx:8` — widgets-card wrapper wiring `useAttachments` + `useUploadAttachmentFiles`.\n- `modules/activities/files/components/AttachmentList.tsx:96` — drag-enter + DropZone for the record page.\n\n### File picker primitives\n- `modules/file-upload/components/FileUploadProvider.tsx:13` + `modules/file-upload/hooks/useFileUpload.ts:4` + `modules/file-upload/contexts/FileUploadContext.ts:5`.\n  - `FileUploadOptions = { multiple?: boolean; accept?: string; onUpload: (files: File[]) => void|Promise<void>; onCancel?: () => void }` (`:5-10`).\n  - `openFileUpload(options)` triggers a hidden `<input type=file>`. Handles the native `cancel` event → `onCancel` (`:57-82`). No progress/retry.\n- `modules/activities/files/components/AttachmentUploadTrigger.tsx:12` — `AttachmentUploadTrigger({ targetableObject, children: ({ openFilePicker }) => ReactNode })`.\n- `modules/activities/files/components/AttachmentFileInput.tsx:17` — `AttachmentFileInput({ ref?, targetableObject, onUploadComplete? })`, hidden `<input type=file multiple>` calling `uploadAttachmentFiles`.\n- `modules/activities/files/components/AttachmentDropdown.tsx` — per-row download/rename/delete menu (see `AttachmentRow.tsx:232`).\n\n### Other upload hooks (all wrap `useDirectFileUpload`, no progress/retry)\n- `modules/activities/emails/hooks/useUploadEmailAttachment.ts:11` — `uploadEmailAttachment(file): Promise<EmailAttachment | null>`, `FileFolder.EmailAttachment`; **enforces `MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE`** with `formatFileSize` snackbar (`:20-29`).\n- `modules/activities/emails/hooks/useUploadEmailImage.ts:40` — `FileFolder.EmailImage`, same size guard (`:29-32`).\n- `modules/workflow/workflow-steps/workflow-actions/hooks/useUploadWorkflowFile.ts:11` — `uploadWorkflowFile(file): Promise<WorkflowAttachment | null>`, `FileFolder.Workflow`, size guard (`:19-26`), reads `size`/`type`/`createdAt` from signed URL result.\n- `modules/ai/hooks/useAiChatFileUpload.ts:12` — `{ uploadFiles: (files: File[]) => Promise<void> }`, `FileFolder.AgentChat`, `Promise.allSettled` + failed-count snackbar, selected-files/uploaded-files Jotai states. No size guard, no retry/cancel.\n- `modules/object-record/record-show/hooks/useRecordImageIdentifierUpload.ts:47` — `FileFolder.FilesField` (avatar image).\n- `modules/front-components/hooks/useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts:529` — `FileFolder.FilesField`.\n\n**Gaps:** no progress bars, no retry, no upload cancellation UI anywhere (only `AbortSignal` plumbed into `useDirectFileUpload` but unused by callers); no storage-quota errors surfaced on the frontend.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Size limits / quota feedback\n\n- `modules/advanced-text-editor/utils/maxAttachmentSize.ts:1` — `export const MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE = 10 * 1024 * 1024;` (the only shared byte-limit constant).\n- `modules/file/utils/formatFileSize.ts:1` — `formatFileSize(size: number): string` (\"1.0 MB\"/\"1.0 KB\"/\"B\"). Test at `modules/file/utils/__tests__/formatFileSize.test.ts`.\n- Size-rejection snackbars (pattern: `File \"${fileName}\" exceeds ${maxUploadSize}`): `useUploadEmailAttachment.ts:20-26`, `useUploadEmailImage.ts:29-33`, `useUploadWorkflowFile.ts:19-24`.\n- `modules/spreadsheet-import/types/SpreadsheetImportDialogOptions.ts:41` — `maxFileSize?: number` supplied through `useSpreadsheetImportInternal()` and enforced by both DropZones. Record-capacity feedback: `SPREADSHEET_MAX_RECORD_IMPORT_CAPACITY` in `spreadsheet-import/constants/SpreadsheetMaxRecordImportCapacity.ts`.\n- No `MAX_FILE_SIZE` symbol, no storage-limit/quota component, and no quota-error handling exist in `twenty-front`.\n\n---\n\n## Supporting utilities & config\n\n- `modules/activities/files/utils/downloadFile.ts:3` — `downloadFile(fullPath, fileName)` (fetch → blob → `file-saver` `saveAs`).\n- `modules/activities/utils/getAttachmentUrl.ts:3` — `getAttachmentUrl({ attachment: AttachmentWithFile }): string` → `attachment.file.url`.\n- `modules/client-config/states/isAttachmentPreviewEnabledState.ts:3` — `isAttachmentPreviewEnabledState` boolean atom (default `false`); gates all preview paths (`FilesDisplay`, `FilesFieldInput`, `AttachmentList`).\n- `~/utils/file/getFileNameAndExtension` (imported at `AttachmentRow.tsx:26`, `DocumentViewer.tsx:19`) — splits name/extension.\n- `modules/ui/field/display/components/GlobalFilePreviewModal.tsx` is mounted once via `WorkspaceAppProviders.tsx:79`, so any component can open the global preview by writing the `filePreviewState` atom.\n\n**Summary of the primary reusable primitives:** `DocumentViewer` (rendering), `GlobalFilePreviewModal` + `filePreviewState` (global modal), `AttachmentList`/`AttachmentRow` (record-page list + local modal), `FilesDisplay`/`FileChip` (field chip), `FileIcon` + `IconMapping` (fallback icons), `useDirectFileUpload` (low-level upload), and `useUploadAttachmentFile(s)` / `useUploadFilesFieldFile` / `useFileUpload` + `DropZone` (upload flows).\n</task_result>\n</task>"
